vway wasu a city within the  state of rio de janeiro in brazil  capitao is the youngest of three  children  raised in a close-knit community held  together by similar social and cultural  ties  there was a lot of support and unity  among the people as everyone tried their  best to help each other where they could  and tried to keep the children out of  gangs and off the street  but ultimately no place was ever truly  safe and soon tragedy and loss  burrowed its way into the sousa family  tearing one of the eldest boys  ruthlessly from this world his murderers  a group of drug dealers with little  remorse of the families they tear apart  time and time again this event would  forever shape the choices and actions  for this family  and no one more so than capital  driven by an intense desire to protect  the people closest to him  he entered the palesia militare where he  trained in a wide range of tactical  weapons  and breaching strategies although he's  very tight-lipped about his past  liaisons  he obviously had a close relationship at  some point as he is the father  of three children his eldest is named  after his brother who passed away  and often the family share stories about  his exploits growing up in order to keep  his memory alive  capitaeo continues the same traditions  that he himself grew up with  family first safer communities together  and open and honest communication with  his children  although he may come across as a little  overbearing at times he struggles to  trust their friends  which is most likely why he encourages  them all to congregate at his home  where he can keep an eye on them he  knows he has raised them to be kind  aware and smart about the choices they  make in their lives  it's more that he has an intense fear of  losing them even more so than other  parents  because of how he tragically lost his  brother he understands that in his line  of work  and in their neighborhood that no one no  matter what is ever truly safe  over time ca